== Method (queue row 4 triage recipe)
Ingress: tb470 eth3 -> x230 port1.0.5 (VLAN 105, vlan105 10.38.215.90/27). Egress: x230 vlan1 10.38.215.29/27 ->
port1.0.2 -> stack sa2 (port1.0.2) -> stack VLAN 1 -> port3.0.13 -> tb470 eth1 (10.38.215.1). Static route
192.0.2.0/24 via 10.38.215.1 (TEST-NET-1, not a real destination). Traffic UDP 10.38.215.65 -> 192.0.2.1 sent to the x230's
MAC with TTL 2, so it reaches eth1 with TTL 1 and tb470 cannot forward it anywhere (no leak off the lab segment).
Counted on eth1 only if the source MAC is the x230's (= routed, not bridged) AND the frame length equals what was sent.
An L2 baseline over the same physical path (port1.0.5 briefly in VLAN 1, bridged) comes first, so any loss can be split
between the path and the routing.

